  methodText:'“Balanced driving distances” minimises the longest individual drive. Ties are resolved by the smaller gap between drives, then the total distance. “Lowest total driving distance” minimises the sum. The app compares a predefined set of candidate towns; a global optimum is not guaranteed. Town centres serve as origins and destinations. OSRM uses accessible road points within 1 km and favours fast routes, which are not necessarily the shortest. These are calculated road distances, not measurements of a completed trip. Regional groups are formed geographically before their meeting places are optimised. “Geographic centre” calculates the equally weighted centre of home locations; straight-line distances are clearly labelled if routing fails. Driving optimisation gives no recommendation without complete routing data. No rail, cost or CO₂ calculation and no live traffic data.',
